We suspected the problem was stiffness in parts of the solution
space.

As to the user-defined sensitivities, I can imagine this'd give you
a speedup.  My understanding there is that you changed the output
of the system function and detected based on size of parameter
state vector, parameter vector, and output.

Rather than overloading the function that way, I'd rather keep everything
explicit so we can provide better error messages and keep more natural data
structures.  But having said that, we have no way to easily return both the
system derivatives and sensitivities with a Stan function.  At least until
we get something like lists or tuples.  Maybe I'll do that next.  I'm
almost done with R/MATLAB-style slicing --- should go in the next release
after the one we're working on now.

I have time to put into the ODE thing now.

- Bob

