Hmmm... after reading over and over the cvs_guide manual I am getting more and more confused if this is really what Stan needs. The so-called forward sensitivity calculate dy/dp_i, i.e. the sensitivity of the system with respect to a parameter. Stan however appears to need a more fine-grained gradient information, i.e. it seems to need this information per equations and per parameter individually while the forward sensitivity calculation gives this information summed over the equations. Sorry for my confusion here, but maybe some more familiar with what is needed could look at equation 2.11 (page 14) of the cvs_guide.pdf - and also consider the adjoint problem 2.16 (page 17).

I am happy to sent the pdf on private communication in order not to spam others.

Sebastian

